    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d970">

                <pb facs="1465" n="1451" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/12–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-04T17:00:00+01:00">December 4, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>214. Reurtel 231, December l.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d970-f1"/> Appreciate your
                    cable. Now that the record has been established, whether war criminals come here
                    or not, we think your line of handling the matter the best that could be taken.
                    Releasing Irish <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> reply to American
                    press without further comment than expressing the wish that the assurances had
                    gone farther was most effective here. More than anything External <pb
                        facs="1466" n="1452" xml:id="pg1452"/> Affairs is apprehensive of
                    unfavorable American press. Eventual possible publication of further
                    representations made to continental neutrals will, we think, have more weight
                    here than direct representations to Eire Government which might be susceptible
                    of interpretation as threats and exploited for local political ends. Whatever
                    Brennan may be instructed to tell you, we place no confidence in any verbal
                    assurances as to De Valera’s intentions. We believe that if he felt it to be his
                    immediate political advantage he would make a point of emphasizing his
                    independence by granting asylum and stand pat on his unequivocal reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
